WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.688
So where should the money
go, and in what order?

2
00:00:02.688 --> 00:00:07.675
The book's chapters line up into five
tiers, cheapest and most certain first.

3
00:00:07.675 --> 00:00:10.463
One: staff time, with no award.

4
00:00:10.463 --> 00:00:15.651
Write the application-to-path policy
that SC-7(4) already asks for.

5
00:00:15.651 --> 00:00:17.862
Instrument a sample of branches.

6
00:00:17.862 --> 00:00:21.751
Fix deterministic egress,
usually a NAT decision.

7
00:00:21.751 --> 00:00:25.375
Register the cleartext
protocols crossing branch links.

8
00:00:25.375 --> 00:00:30.900
And test, not just read, that DNS
reaches CISA's Protective DNS.

9
00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:32.575
Two: requirements time.

10
00:00:32.575 --> 00:00:38.112
Put the target attributes
into the BOD 26-02 refresh.

11
00:00:38.112 --> 00:00:41.012
Three: accreditation and CLAW onboarding.

12
00:00:41.012 --> 00:00:45.859
The field-office case calls accreditation,
not procurement, the critical path;

13
00:00:45.859 --> 00:00:48.021
circuits arrive in about a quarter,

14
00:00:48.021 --> 00:00:51.451
an authorized breakout
architecture takes far longer.

15
00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:53.412
Four: protect the governor.

16
00:00:53.412 --> 00:01:00.214
Phishing-resistant MFA, a hardened baseline,
patching inside BOD 26-04's windows,

17
00:01:00.214 --> 00:01:05.263
the shortest of which is three
days, and logs held off the box.

18
00:01:05.263 --> 00:01:07.875
Five, and only then: capital.

19
00:01:07.875 --> 00:01:11.706
Hubs first, then office waves
timed to MPLS contract renewals,

20
00:01:11.706 --> 00:01:16.213
scoped to the branches and applications
where measurement says it pays.

21
00:01:16.213 --> 00:01:18.525
The panel on the right is about pricing.

22
00:01:18.525 --> 00:01:23.976
Moving from MPLS to internet access plus
a cloud security service changes the cost

23
00:01:23.976 --> 00:01:29.111
variable from site count and port speed
to user count, and the per-user security

24
00:01:29.111 --> 00:01:34.325
subscription is the line most likely to
dominate, and the one most often left out.

25
00:01:34.325 --> 00:01:40.088
Price your own circuits in GSA's EIS pricer
rather than citing a marketing multiple.

26
00:01:40.088 --> 00:01:43.134
And don't justify the
program on latency alone;

27
00:01:43.134 --> 00:01:46.500
the stronger argument is
governance and evidence.

28
00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:49.732
The sponsor and CIO set
scope, funding and sequence,

29
00:01:49.732 --> 00:01:54.860
and this order needs to be settled before
the next September budget submission.
